🌐 How HTTP Client-Server Communication Works.?

💥What is HTTP:
 → HTTP stands for HyperText Transfer Protocol.
 → It’s the foundation of communication on the web the protocol used for transferring data between a client (browser) and a server.

✅ Why is HTTP important:
💬 Enables communication between users and websites
📄 Transfers web pages, images, videos, and data
📡 Uses requests and responses to deliver content

🔄 How HTTP Works  :
→ A client (like your web browser) makes a request for example, when you type www.amazon.com and hit Enter.
→ The request travels over the internet to reach the web server.
→ The server receives it, processes the request (maybe fetches data from a database), and sends back an HTTP response.
→ Your browser receives the response (HTML, CSS, JavaScript) and renders the webpage.

💡 Real-Life Example:
 Imagine you’re ordering pizza online🍕:
 → You (the client) place an order via the website.
 → The restaurant’s backend system (the server) receives and confirms it.
 → A delivery update (response) is sent back to you🛵
 → And just like that, HTTP enables this interaction between user and web services!
